      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a lot of specific variables. honestly, some of my managers are worried that focusing too much on things like non-native speakers or housing projects might be seen as unfair or biased if they eventually have to justify why certain loans were denied. but from a purely data-driven risk perspective, if you had to rank those, which ones correlate most strongly with a neighborhood losing its economic stability or seeing its commercial tax base erode?",
